    "block": "<h2>About Sports For Life — Value Added Course at Delhi University</h2>\n<p>Offered as a Value Added Course (VAC) under DU's UGCF/NEP, Sports For Life carries 2 credits and is open to all programmes as a common pool paper, most often in Sem 1-2. Broad VAC overview. This page brings together syllabus, previous year papers and study material so you can see the taught order and exam pattern together.</p>\n<p><strong>What you will study (broad UGCF outline — verify from your college):</strong> The DU syllabus is organised into four units. For Sports For Life, the broad coverage is:</p>\n<ul style=\"margin:8px 0 8px 18px\"><li><strong>Unit 1:</strong> Unit 1: Foundations & concepts</li><li><strong>Unit 2:</strong> Unit 2: Applied theory & examples</li><li><strong>Unit 3:</strong> Unit 3: Contemporary issues & case studies</li><li><strong>Unit 4:</strong> Unit 4: Practice, field work & evaluation</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Exam pattern & marking:</strong> Typically 2 credits, evaluated via continuous assessment, assignments, presentations and a 50-75 marks semester-end theory/practical paper. Questions are short notes (5 marks) and applied long answers (10 marks) from the four units, plus field work or community engagement for many VACs. Examiners look for unit-wise structure, one relevant example per answer, and a clear conclusion.</p>\n<p><strong>How to prepare & what is missing:</strong> Start with Units 1-4 above, then solve the PYQs shown on this page to mark which unit each question came from. That mapping tells you which units repeat most (usually the middle units). Right now the IMP questions / detailed notes PDF for this paper may not be uploaded yet — the list below shows what is currently available. Once your college or the admin uploads the official IMP Q&A PDF, it will automatically appear above with an <em>IMP Q</em> tag.</p>\n<div style=\"background:rgba(30,95,255,.06);border-left:3px solid #1E5FFF;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;margin:14px 0\"><strong>Please verify:</strong> DU's Value Added Course syllabus and paper codes can vary slightly by college and semester. Confirm the exact unit list and credit distribution from your college's official syllabus PDF and department notice. The overview above is a broad guide from the UGCF structure — the precise, verified IMP PDF will be uploaded shortly and will replace this placeholder reference.</div>\n<p>Official sources: <a href=\"https://www.du.ac.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">University of Delhi</a> · <a href=\"http://exam.du.ac.in\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DU Exam Portal</a> · your college's Value Added Course handout.</p>",
